Spec: Native Windows owned-runtime test host

Purpose:
  Prove actual frpc process and private IPC identity without exporting device keys or altering installed services.

Owns:
  ./FrpAuthority.Tests.csproj
  ./Program.cs

Structure:
  ./AndroidFixture.cs: Optional isolated emulator Keystore and actual private runtime coordination.

Must:
  In scoped-only mode discover approved publishers automatically and verify publisher revocation cleanup without launching static publisher or visitor profiles.
  Provide a scoped-runtime-only mode that reuses the actual SDK fixture without rerunning static-route or Android suites; derive its visitor configuration on demand.
  On failure retain only exception type and bounded method names for local debugging, never messages, arguments or raw stack paths.
  Include the Windows formal SDK fixture only in Windows-only runs and account for its additional business sockets; preserve separate Android evidence.
  Derive runtime namespace and configuration from explicitly approved fixture applications and fixed loopback targets.
  Test real file bytes, blocked relay revocation and local approval lifecycle with bounded cleanup of only owned processes, sockets, files and CNG keys.
  Emit fixed aggregate results only, without raw diagnostics, private keys or credentials.
  Mark each run pending before starting and preserve a separate aggregate result for success or failure so stale passing output cannot stand in for a failed retry.
  Compose the real SDK, inner Agent data mTLS and exact local/server service grants through actual FRP relay; verify missing local authority and scope recombination fail before backend delivery.
  Exercise an XTCP-only visitor with relay fallback disabled and real loopback STUN observations; verify actual SDK business bytes and active direct revocation separately from physical NAT acceptance.

  Count actual Android SDK backend connections separately from internal bridge proof and retain both results.

  Explicitly configure both loopback STUN destinations and reject malformed endpoint lists before launching any child.
  Include formal Android connection fixture business sockets in the actual backend count and keep simulated generation changes separate from physical network acceptance.
